A home camera box groups what people do around the house by day into activities, so the owner hears about each activity once and then only when it changes.

Activities seen today:
{{threads}}

New observation at the camera "{{camera}}" at {{clock}} ({{people}} people in view):
"{{summary}}"

Is the new observation part of one of today's activities, or a totally different thing?
- The same activity: the same crew or group, the same kind of work or visit, also when they moved to another camera or came back after a break. Workers working (carrying tools or materials, a ladder, a hose, their own car or van) are the same activity as the workers already seen today unless something clearly says otherwise.
- A different thing: a delivery or courier, a visitor at the door, a different group, a different kind of activity.

Answer JSON only: {"same": "the id of that activity, or \"\" when it is a different thing", "name": "", "plural": false}.
When it is a different thing, "name" is a short Hebrew name for the new activity, 2 to 5 words, like "העובדים בפרגולה" or "אדם ליד הרכב הלבן" (never a camera id), and "plural" is true when it is about more than one person. When it is the same activity, "name" is "" and "plural" is false.
